%S A117687 0,1,100,8649,10000,59049,88209,91809,104976,106929,110889,207936,
%T A117687 257049,318096,321489,349281,356409,363609,370881,381924,396900,
%U A117687 400689,404496,419904,480249,488601,492804,497025,514089,527076,549081,558009,567009
%N A117687 Squares for which both the sum of the digits and the product of the digits are cubes.
%C A117687 If k is a term then so is 100*k. - _Robert Israel_, Aug 10 2026
%D A117687 Elena Deza and Michel Marie Deza, Figurate numbers, World Scientific Publishing (2012), page 422.
%H A117687 Robert Israel, <a href="/A117687/b117687.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A117687 321489 is in the sequence because it is a square and (1)the sum of its digits 3+2+1+4+8+9=27 is a cube and (2)the product of its digits 3*2*1*4*8*9=1728 is also a cube.
%e A117687 396900 = 630^2 is in the sequence since 3+9+6+9+0+0 = 27 and 3*9*6*9*0*0 = 0 are cubes.
%p A117687 filter:= proc(k) local L;
%p A117687   L:= convert(k,base,10);
%p A117687   surd(convert(L,`+`),3)::integer and surd(convert(L,`*`),3)::integer
%p A117687 end proc:
%p A117687 select(filter, [seq(i^2,i=0..2000)]); # _Robert Israel_, Aug 10 2026
%Y A117687 Cf. A000290, A000578, A004159, A053667.
